blueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:1227:	By induction on $k$. The case $k = 0$ follows directly from Definition~\ref{def:cl-func}, since then $L = 0$ and $T$ acts by the single $\ell$-level function $R_0$ on the register subspace $V$. For the inductive step, write $L(x^U) = x^{L_1} + L_{>1,\,x^{L_1}}(x^{U_{>1}})$ with complementary register subspaces $U_1$ and $U_{>1}$ of $U$. For each value $x^{L_1}$, the function $T_{>1,\,x^{L_1}}$ on $U_{>1} \oplus V$ sending $x^{U_{>1} \oplus V}$ to $L_{>1,\,x^{L_1}}(x^{U_{>1}}) + R_{x^{L_1} + x^{L_{>1}}}(x^V)$ is the concatenation of the $(k-1)$-level function $L_{>1,\,x^{L_1}}$ with a family drawn from $\{R_u\}$, hence is $(k+\ell-1)$-level by the induction hypothesis. The claim then follows from Definition~\ref{def:cl-func} applied with first subspace $U_1$ and first linear map $L_1$.
