{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree.lean'","aggregated_output":"     1\timport MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.LowDegreeGameTheorems\n     2\timport MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.PauliBasisTest\n     3\t\n     4\t/-!\n     5\t# The directly indexed low-degree game\n     6\t\n     7\tThe low-degree game used by the Pauli-basis combining argument is needed in\n     8\tdimension `2 * m + 2`.  The existing conditionally linear game represents a\n     9\tcoordinate index by an equally sized fiber in the scalar field and therefore\n    10\trequires the dimension to divide the field size.  This file gives the separate\n    11\tdirectly indexed variant which samples that index directly.\n    12\t\n    13\tThe geometric line carrier records the sampled coordinate, and line evaluation\n    14\tuses an `Option` outcome rather than assigning a value when a point does not\n    15\tdetermine one.  The game retains the point, axis-line, and diagonal-line answer\n    16\tformats and the nine ordered type branches of the original low-degree game.\n    17\t\n    18\t## References\n    19\t\n    20\tThe underlying game is `def:ld-game` in\n    21\t`blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:17-105`, with source origin\n    22\t`references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:31-391`.\n    23\tThe need for the directly indexed repair in Chapter 15 is explained around\n    24\t`rem:qld-4-7-divisibility` in\n    25\t`blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1257-1293` and in\n    26\t`docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility.tex`.\n    27\t-/\n    28\t\n    29\topen scoped BigOperators\n    30\t\n    31\tnamespace MIPStarRE.QPBT\n    32\t\n    33\topen MIPStarRE.LDT\n    34\topen MIPStarRE.LDT.Preliminaries\n    35\topen MIPStarRE.Quantum\n    36\t\n    37\tnoncomputable section\n    38\t\n    39\t/-- Parameters for the directly indexed low-degree game.  Unlike `LdParams`,\n    40\tthis directly indexed line-space construction has no divisibility field: its coordinate index is\n    41\tsampled from `Fin m` rather than encoded by fibers of `chiIndex`.\n    42\t\n    43\tThis is the direct-index repair described in\n    44\t`docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility.tex`; it is not a second\n    45\tdefinition of the source verifier game. -/\n    46\tstructure DirectLdParams where\n    47\t  q : ℕ\n    48\t  m : ℕ\n    49\t  d : ℕ\n    50\t  k : ℕ\n    51\t  hm : 1 ≤ m\n    52\t  hd : 1 ≤ d\n    53\t  hk : 1 ≤ k\n    54\t  hq : IsAdmissibleSize q\n    55\t\n    56\t/-- The canonical scalar model for directly indexed parameters. -/\n    57\tnoncomputable def DirectLdParams.model (D : DirectLdParams) : FixedFieldModel D.q :=\n    58\t  fixedFieldModel D.q D.hq\n    59\t\n    60\t/-- The scalar field of a directly indexed low-degree game. -/\n    61\tabbrev DirectScalarQ (D : DirectLdParams) := D.model.K\n    62\t\n    63\t/-- The first coordinate, available because directly indexed dimensions are\n    64\tpositive. -/\n    65\tdef DirectLdParams.firstIndex (D : DirectLdParams) : Fin D.m :=\n    66\t  ⟨0, lt_of_lt_of_le Nat.zero_lt_one D.hm⟩\n    67\t\n    68\tinstance (D : DirectLdParams) : Nonempty (Fin D.m) := ⟨D.firstIndex⟩\n    69\t\n    70\t/-- The direct game used at the extended dimension of the combining map.  Its\n    71\tfield, degree, and simultaneity parameters are inherited from `P`, while its\n    72\tdimension is `2 * P.m + 2`; no divisibility assertion is introduced.\n    73\t\n    74\tThe construction has dimension `2 * P.m + 2` without requiring\n    75\t`2 * P.m + 2 ∣ P.q`; it supplies the directly indexed line and coordinate\n    76\tspaces used in the dimension-extension argument of\n    77\t`blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1257-1293`.\n    78\t-/\n    79\tdef AdmissibleParams.extendedDirectLd (P : AdmissibleParams) : DirectLdParams where\n    80\t  q := P.q\n    81\t  m := 2 * P.m + 2\n    82\t  d := P.d\n    83\t  k := 1\n    84\t  hm := by omega\n    85\t  hd := P.hd\n    86\t  hk := by decide\n    87\t  hq := P.hq\n    88\t\n    89\t/-- A common random sample for the directly indexed question distribution.\n    90\tThe point, coordinate index, and unrestricted direction are mutually uniform. -/\n    91\tstructure DirectLdSpace (D : DirectLdParams) where\n    92\t  point : Fin D.m → DirectScalarQ D\n    93\t  index : Fin D.m\n    94\t  direction : Fin D.m → DirectScalarQ D\n    95\t  deriving DecidableEq, Fintype\n    96\t\n    97\tinstance (D : DirectLdParams) : Nonempty (DirectLdSpace D) :=\n    98\t  ⟨⟨0, D.firstIndex, 0⟩⟩\n    99\t\n   100\t/-- Zero the coordinates preceding the directly sampled prefix index. -/\n   101\tdef directPrefixProjection {D : DirectLdParams} (i : Fin D.m)\n   102\t    (v : Fin D.m → DirectScalarQ D) : Fin D.m → DirectScalarQ D :=\n   103\t  fun j => if j.val < i.val then 0 else v j\n   104\t\n   105\t/-- Canonical line descriptions whose coordinate index is stored directly.\n   106\tCoordinates are numbered from zero, so `index = i` represents coordinate\n   107\t`i + 1` in the paper. -/\n   108\tinductive DirectLineDesc (D : DirectLdParams) where\n   109\t  | axis (base : Fin D.m → DirectScalarQ D) (index : Fin D.m)\n   110\t      (baseFixed : lineRepMap (coordinateDirection index) base = base)\n   111\t  | diagonal (base : Fin D.m → DirectScalarQ D) (index : Fin D.m)\n   112\t      (direction : Fin D.m → DirectScalarQ D)\n   113\t      (baseFixed : lineRepMap direction base = base)\n   114\t      (prefixZero : ∀ j : Fin D.m, j.val < index.val → direction j = 0)\n   115\t  deriving DecidableEq\n   116\t\n   117\t/-- The kind of a directly indexed line. -/\n   118\tdef DirectLineDesc.kind {D : DirectLdParams} : DirectLineDesc D → LineKind\n   119\t  | .axis _ _ _ => .axis\n   120\t  | .diagonal _ _ _ _ _ => .diagonal\n   121\t\n   122\t/-- The coordinate index stored in a directly indexed line. -/\n   123\tdef DirectLineDesc.index {D : DirectLdParams} : DirectLineDesc D → Fin D.m\n   124\t  | .axis _ index _ => index\n   125\t  | .diagonal _ index _ _ _ => index\n   126\t\n   127\t/-- The canonical base point of a directly indexed line. -/\n   128\tdef DirectLineDesc.base {D : DirectLdParams} :\n   129\t    DirectLineDesc D → Fin D.m → DirectScalarQ D\n   130\t  | .axis base _ _ => base\n   131\t  | .diagonal base _ _ _ _ => base\n   132\t\n   133\t/-- The geometric direction of a directly indexed line. -/\n   134\tdef DirectLineDesc.direction {D : DirectLdParams} (line : DirectLineDesc D) :\n   135\t    Fin D.m → DirectScalarQ D :=\n   136\t  match line with\n   137\t  | .axis _ index _ => coordinateDirection index\n   138\t  | .diagonal _ _ direction _ _ => direction\n   139\t\n   140\t/-- The base of a directly indexed description is fixed by its geometric\n   141\tdirection. -/\n   142\ttheorem DirectLineDesc.base_fixed {D : DirectLdParams} (line : DirectLineDesc D) :\n   143\t    lineRepMap line.direction line.base = line.base := by\n   144\t  cases line with\n   145\t  | axis base index baseFixed => exact baseFixed\n   146\t  | diagonal base index direction baseFixed prefixZero => exact baseFixed\n   147\t\n   148\t/-- Every directly indexed diagonal description retains its prefix-zero\n   149\tinvariant. -/\n   150\ttheorem DirectLineDesc.diagonal_prefix_zero {D : DirectLdParams}\n   151\t    (line : DirectLineDesc D) (hline : line.kind = .diagonal) :\n   152\t    ∀ j : Fin D.m, j.val < line.index.val → line.direction j = 0 := by\n   153\t  cases line with\n   154\t  | axis base index baseFixed => simp [DirectLineDesc.kind] at hline\n   155\t  | diagonal base index direction baseFixed prefixZero => exact prefixZero\n   156\t\n   157\t/-- The point set represented by a directly indexed line. -/\n   158\tnoncomputable def DirectLineDesc.pointSet {D : DirectLdParams}\n   159\t    (line : DirectLineDesc D) : Set (Fin D.m → DirectScalarQ D) :=\n   160\t  linePoints line.base line.direction\n   161\t\n   162\t/-- Turn a direct sample into its canonical axis-line description. -/\n   163\tnoncomputable def directALineDescOf (D : DirectLdParams)\n   164\t    (sample : DirectLdSpace D) : DirectLineDesc D :=\n   165\t  let direction := coordinateDirection sample.index\n   166\t  let base := lineRepMap direction sample.point\n   167\t  .axis base sample.index (lineRepMap_apply_self direction sample.point)\n   168\t\n   169\t/-- Turn a direct sample into its canonical diagonal-line description. -/\n   170\tnoncomputable def directDLineDescOf (D : DirectLdParams)\n   171\t    (sample : DirectLdSpace D) : DirectLineDesc D :=\n   172\t  let direction := directPrefixProjection sample.index sample.direction\n   173\t  let base := lineRepMap direction sample.point\n   174\t  .diagonal base sample.index direction\n   175\t    (lineRepMap_apply_self direction sample.point) (by\n   176\t      intro j hj\n   177\t      change directPrefixProjection sample.index sample.direction j = 0\n   178\t      rw [directPrefixProjection, if_pos hj])\n   179\t\n   180\t/-- The axis-line/point law with a directly sampled coordinate index. -/\n   181\tnoncomputable def directALinePointDist (D : DirectLdParams) :\n   182\t    Distribution (DirectLineDesc D × (Fin D.m → DirectScalarQ D)) :=\n   183\t  (uniformDistribution (DirectLdSpace D)).map fun sample =>\n   184\t    (directALineDescOf D sample, sample.point)\n   185\t\n   186\t/-- The diagonal-line/point law with a directly sampled prefix index. -/\n   187\tnoncomputable def directDLinePointDist (D : DirectLdParams) :\n   188\t    Distribution (DirectLineDesc D × (Fin D.m → DirectScalarQ D)) :=\n   189\t  (uniformDistribution (DirectLdSpace D)).map fun sample =>\n   190\t    (directDLineDescOf D sample, sample.point)\n   191\t\n   192\t/-- The equal mixture of the directly indexed axis and diagonal line-point\n   193\tlaws.  This is the replacement for the otherwise undefined extended-dimension\n   194\tinstance used at paper\n   195\t`references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1020-1116`. -/\n   196\tnoncomputable def directLinePointDist (D : DirectLdParams) :\n   197\t    Distribution (DirectLineDesc D × (Fin D.m → DirectScalarQ D)) :=\n   198\t  Distribution.mix (1 / 2) (by norm_num) (by norm_num)\n   199\t    (directALinePointDist D) (directDLinePointDist D)\n   200\t\n   201\t/-- The directly indexed axis-line/point law is probabilistic. -/\n   202\ttheorem directALinePointDist_isProbability (D : DirectLdParams) :\n   203\t    (directALinePointDist D).IsProbability := by\n   204\t  exact (uniformDistribution_isProbability (DirectLdSpace D)).map _\n   205\t\n   206\t/-- The directly indexed diagonal-line/point law is probabilistic. -/\n   207\ttheorem directDLinePointDist_isProbability (D : DirectLdParams) :\n   208\t    (directDLinePointDist D).IsProbability := by\n   209\t  exact (uniformDistribution_isProbability (DirectLdSpace D)).map _\n   210\t\n   211\t/-- The directly indexed line-point mixture is probabilistic. -/\n   212\ttheorem directLinePointDist_isProbability (D : DirectLdParams) :\n   213\t    (directLinePointDist D).IsProbability := by\n   214\t  exact Distribution.mix_isProbability _ _ _\n   215\t    (directALinePointDist_isProbability D) (directDLinePointDist_isProbability D)\n   216\t    (by norm_num) (by norm_num)\n   217\t\n   218\t/-- The point and stored-index marginals of the direct axis-line law are\n   219\tuniform.  This is a direct-index analogue of `lem:alnf`, required by\n   220\tthe repair described in `docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility.tex`;\n   221\tthe source distribution is at\n   222\t`references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:243-257`.\n   223\t-/\n   224\ttheorem directALinePointDist_point_index_marginal_uniform (D : DirectLdParams) :\n   225\t    (directALinePointDist D).map Prod.snd =\n   226\t        uniformDistribution (Fin D.m → DirectScalarQ D) ∧\n   227\t      (directALinePointDist D).map (fun sample => sample.1.index) =\n   228\t        uniformDistribution (Fin D.m) := by\n   229\t  sorry\n   230\t\n   231\t/-- Every sampled direct axis line contains its paired point.  This is the\n   232\tDirect-index incidence obligation corresponding to `lem:alnf` and\n   233\tthe repair in `docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility.tex`. -/\n   234\ttheorem directALinePointDist_mem_line (D : DirectLdParams) :\n   235\t    ∀ sample ∈ (directALinePointDist D).support,\n   236\t      sample.2 ∈ sample.1.pointSet := by\n   237\t  sorry\n   238\t\n   239\t/-- The point and stored-index marginals of the direct diagonal-line law are\n   240\tuniform.  This is the direct-index analogue of `lem:dlnf`, paper\n   241\t`references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:261-272`,\n   242\tand is a named obligation in the dimension-divisibility repair. -/\n   243\ttheorem directDLinePointDist_point_index_marginal_uniform (D : DirectLdParams) :\n   244\t    (directDLinePointDist D).map Prod.snd =\n   245\t        uniformDistribution (Fin D.m → DirectScalarQ D) ∧\n   246\t      (directDLinePointDist D).map (fun sample => sample.1.index) =\n   247\t        uniformDistribution (Fin D.m) := by\n   248\t  sorry\n   249\t\n   250\t/-- Every sampled direct diagonal line contains its paired point.  This is the\n   251\tDirect-index incidence obligation corresponding to `lem:dlnf`. -/\n   252\ttheorem directDLinePointDist_mem_line (D : DirectLdParams) :\n   253\t    ∀ sample ∈ (directDLinePointDist D).support,\n   254\t      sample.2 ∈ sample.1.pointSet := by\n   255\t  sorry\n   256\t\n   257\t/-- A sampled direct diagonal direction vanishes below its stored prefix\n   258\tindex.  This is the direct counterpart of the third conclusion of\n   259\t`lem:dlnf`, paper\n   260\t`references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:261-272`.\n   261\t-/\n   262\ttheorem directDLinePointDist_prefix_zero (D : DirectLdParams) :\n   263\t    ∀ sample ∈ (directDLinePointDist D).support,\n   264\t      ∀ j : Fin D.m, j.val < sample.1.index.val →\n   265\t        sample.1.direction j = 0 := by\n   266\t  sorry\n   267\t\n   268\t/-- Coefficient lists for a univariate polynomial of degree at most `c` in the\n   269\tdirect scalar field. -/\n   270\tabbrev DirectDegPoly (D : DirectLdParams) (c : ℕ) :=\n   271\t  Fin (c + 1) → DirectScalarQ D\n   272\t\n   273\t/-- A direct line polynomial evaluates to `a` at `u` when `u` lies on the line\n   274\tand every parameter presenting `u` gives value `a`.  The universal clause\n   275\tkeeps the zero-direction case explicit. -/\n   276\tdef DirectEvaluatesTo {D : DirectLdParams} {c : ℕ} (line : DirectLineDesc D)\n   277\t    (f : DirectDegPoly D c) (u : Fin D.m → DirectScalarQ D)\n   278\t    (a : DirectScalarQ D) : Prop :=\n   279\t  (∃ t : DirectScalarQ D, u = line.base + t • line.direction) ∧\n   280\t    ∀ t : DirectScalarQ D, u = line.base + t • line.direction →\n   281\t      evalCoefficient f t = a\n   282\t\n   283\t/-- Option-completed evaluation of a direct line polynomial.  `none` is an\n   284\texplicit outcome when the point does not determine an evaluation; no field\n   285\tvalue is used as a fallback. -/\n   286\tnoncomputable def directEvalOpt {D : DirectLdParams} {c : ℕ}\n   287\t    (line : DirectLineDesc D) (u : Fin D.m → DirectScalarQ D)\n   288\t    (f : DirectDegPoly D c) : Option (DirectScalarQ D) := by\n   289\t  classical\n   290\t  exact if h : ∃ a : DirectScalarQ D, DirectEvaluatesTo line f u a then\n   291\t    some (Classical.choose h)\n   292\t  else none\n   293\t\n   294\t/-- The typed question alphabet of the directly indexed game. -/\n   295\tabbrev DirectLdQuestion (D : DirectLdParams) := LdType × DirectLdSpace D\n   296\t\n   297\t/-- Canonicalize a common direct sample for one question type.  Irrelevant\n   298\tcoordinates are fixed, so point questions reveal no sampled line index and\n   299\taxis-line questions reveal no diagonal direction. -/\n   300\tnoncomputable def directLdMap (D : DirectLdParams) :\n   301\t    LdType → DirectLdSpace D → DirectLdSpace D\n   302\t  | .point, sample => ⟨sample.point, D.firstIndex, 0⟩\n   303\t  | .aline, sample =>\n   304\t      let direction := coordinateDirection sample.index\n   305\t      ⟨lineRepMap direction sample.point, sample.index, 0⟩\n   306\t  | .dline, sample =>\n   307\t      let direction := directPrefixProjection sample.index sample.direction\n   308\t      ⟨lineRepMap direction sample.point, sample.index, direction⟩\n   309\t\n   310\t/-- The directly indexed question distribution.  It has the same uniform\n   311\tordered type-pair branches as `ldQuestionDistribution`, but its common sample\n   312\tcontains an actual coordinate index rather than a field seed. -/\n   313\tnoncomputable def directLdQuestionDistribution (D : DirectLdParams) :\n   314\t    Distribution (DirectLdQuestion D × DirectLdQuestion D) :=\n   315\t  (uniformDistribution ((LdType × LdType) × DirectLdSpace D)).map fun sample =>\n   316\t    ((sample.1.1, directLdMap D sample.1.1 sample.2),\n   317\t      (sample.1.2, directLdMap D sample.1.2 sample.2))\n   318\t\n   319\t/-- The directly indexed question law is probabilistic. -/\n   320\ttheorem directLdQuestionDistribution_isProbability (D : DirectLdParams) :\n   321\t    (directLdQuestionDistribution D).IsProbability := by\n   322\t  exact (uniformDistribution_isProbability\n   323\t    ((LdType × LdType) × DirectLdSpace D)).map _\n   324\t\n   325\t/-- The answer alphabet of the directly indexed game. -/\n   326\tinductive DirectLdAnswer (D : DirectLdParams) where\n   327\t  | pointVals (a : Fin D.k → DirectScalarQ D)\n   328\t  | alinePolys (a : Fin D.k → Fin (D.d + 1) → DirectScalarQ D)\n   329\t  | dlinePolys (a : Fin D.k → Fin (D.m * D.d + 1) → DirectScalarQ D)\n   330\t  deriving DecidableEq\n   331\t\n   332\t/-- A finite code for the directly indexed answer alphabet. -/\n   333\tabbrev DirectLdAnswerCode (D : DirectLdParams) :=\n   334\t  (Fin D.k → DirectScalarQ D) ⊕\n   335\t    ((Fin D.k → Fin (D.d + 1) → DirectScalarQ D) ⊕\n   336\t      (Fin D.k → Fin (D.m * D.d + 1) → DirectScalarQ D))\n   337\t\n   338\t/-- Constructor-preserving equivalence between the inductive answer type and\n   339\tits finite code. -/\n   340\tnoncomputable def directLdAnswerEquiv (D : DirectLdParams) :\n   341\t    DirectLdAnswer D ≃ DirectLdAnswerCode D where\n   342\t  toFun\n   343\t    | .pointVals a => .inl a\n   344\t    | .alinePolys a => .inr (.inl a)\n   345\t    | .dlinePolys a => .inr (.inr a)\n   346\t  invFun\n   347\t    | .inl a => .pointVals a\n   348\t    | .inr (.inl a) => .alinePolys a\n   349\t    | .inr (.inr a) => .dlinePolys a\n   350\t  left_inv := by intro answer; cases answer <;> rfl\n   351\t  right_inv := by\n   352\t    intro answer\n   353\t    rcases answer with a | a\n   354\t    · rfl\n   355\t    · rcases a with a | a <;> rfl\n   356\t\n   357\tinstance (D : DirectLdParams) : Inhabited (DirectLdAnswer D) :=\n   358\t  ⟨.pointVals 0⟩\n   359\t\n   360\tnoncomputable instance (D : DirectLdParams) : Fintype (DirectLdAnswer D) :=\n   361\t  Fintype.ofEquiv (DirectLdAnswerCode D) (directLdAnswerEquiv D).symm\n   362\t\n   363\t/-- Check that a direct-game answer has the constructor required by its\n   364\tquestion type. -/\n   365\tdef validDirectLdAnswer {D : DirectLdParams} (t : LdType)\n   366\t    (answer : DirectLdAnswer D) : Bool :=\n   367\t  match t, answer with\n   368\t  | .point, .pointVals _ => true\n   369\t  | .aline, .alinePolys _ => true\n   370\t  | .dline, .dlinePolys _ => true\n   371\t  | _, _ => false\n   372\t\n   373\t/-- The directly indexed axis-line versus point acceptance relation. -/\n   374\tdef directAlinePointCondition (D : DirectLdParams)\n   375\t    (line point : DirectLdSpace D)\n   376\t    (f : Fin D.k → Fin (D.d + 1) → DirectScalarQ D)\n   377\t    (a : Fin D.k → DirectScalarQ D) : Prop :=\n   378\t  ∀ t : DirectScalarQ D,\n   379\t    point.point = line.point + t • coordinateDirection line.index →\n   380\t      ∀ j : Fin D.k, evalCoefficient (f j) t = a j\n   381\t\n   382\t/-- The directly indexed diagonal-line versus point acceptance relation. -/\n   383\tdef directDlinePointCondition (D : DirectLdParams)\n   384\t    (line point : DirectLdSpace D)\n   385\t    (f : Fin D.k → Fin (D.m * D.d + 1) → DirectScalarQ D)\n   386\t    (a : Fin D.k → DirectScalarQ D) : Prop :=\n   387\t  ∀ t : DirectScalarQ D,\n   388\t    point.point = line.point + t • line.direction →\n   389\t      ∀ j : Fin D.k, evalCoefficient (f j) t = a j\n   390\t\n   391\t/-- The directly indexed low-degree win predicate.  It differs from\n   392\t`ldWinPredicate` only by reading the coordinate index directly from each line\n   393\tquestion. -/\n   394\tnoncomputable def directLdWinPredicate (D : DirectLdParams) :\n   395\t    DirectLdQuestion D → DirectLdQuestion D →\n   396\t      DirectLdAnswer D → DirectLdAnswer D → Bool :=\n   397\t  open Classical in\n   398\t  fun (tA, xA) (tB, xB) a b =>\n   399\t    if validDirectLdAnswer tA a && validDirectLdAnswer tB b then\n   400\t      match tA, tB, a, b with\n   401\t      | .point, .point, .pointVals u, .pointVals v => decide (u = v)\n   402\t      | .aline, .point, .alinePolys f, .pointVals u =>\n   403\t          decide (directAlinePointCondition D xA xB f u)\n   404\t      | .point, .aline, .pointVals u, .alinePolys f =>\n   405\t          decide (directAlinePointCondition D xB xA f u)\n   406\t      | .dline, .point, .dlinePolys f, .pointVals u =>\n   407\t          decide (directDlinePointCondition D xA xB f u)\n   408\t      | .point, .dline, .pointVals u, .dlinePolys f =>\n   409\t          decide (directDlinePointCondition D xB xA f u)\n   410\t      | .aline, .aline, .alinePolys f, .alinePolys g => decide (f = g)\n   411\t      | .dline, .dline, .dlinePolys f, .dlinePolys g => decide (f = g)\n   412\t      | _, _, _, _ => true\n   413\t    else false\n   414\t\n   415\t/-- The directly indexed low-degree game at an arbitrary positive dimension.\n   416\tIt is an internal analysis game, not the conditionally linear verifier game\n   417\t`ldGame`. -/\n   418\tnoncomputable def directLdGame (D : DirectLdParams) : Game where\n   419\t  QuestionA := DirectLdQuestion D\n   420\t  QuestionB := DirectLdQuestion D\n   421\t  AnswerA := DirectLdAnswer D\n   422\t  AnswerB := DirectLdAnswer D\n   423\t  μ := directLdQuestionDistribution D\n   424\t  μ_prob := directLdQuestionDistribution_isProbability D\n   425\t  decide := directLdWinPredicate D\n   426\t\n   427\t/-- The canonical point question associated with a geometric point. -/\n   428\tdef directLdPointQuestionOf (D : DirectLdParams)\n   429\t    (u : Fin D.m → DirectScalarQ D) : DirectLdQuestion D :=\n   430\t  (.point, ⟨u, D.firstIndex, 0⟩)\n   431\t\n   432\t/-- Total point-answer relabeling used in the direct soundness conclusion.\n   433\tWrong-form answers are folded into the zero tuple, exactly as for\n   434\t`ldPointValuesOrZero`. -/\n   435\tdef directLdPointValuesOrZero (D : DirectLdParams) :\n   436\t    DirectLdAnswer D → Fin D.k → DirectScalarQ D\n   437\t  | .pointVals values => values\n   438\t  | .alinePolys _ => 0\n   439\t  | .dlinePolys _ => 0\n   440\t\n   441\t/-- A simultaneous tuple of bounded polynomials for the directly indexed\n   442\tgame. -/\n   443\tnoncomputable abbrev DirectPolyTuple (D : DirectLdParams) :=\n   444\t  Fin D.k → PolyIndex D.m (DirectScalarQ D) D.d\n   445\t\n   446\t/-- A polynomial-tuple POVM for the directly indexed game. -/\n   447\tnoncomputable abbrev DirectPolyMeasTuple (D : DirectLdParams) (ι : Type*)\n   448\t    [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] :=\n   449\t  Measurement (DirectPolyTuple D) ι\n   450\t\n   451\t/-- Evaluate every component of a direct polynomial tuple at a point. -/\n   452\tdef evalDirectPolyTupleAt {D : DirectLdParams}\n   453\t    (u : Fin D.m → DirectScalarQ D) (g : DirectPolyTuple D) :\n   454\t    Fin D.k → DirectScalarQ D :=\n   455\t  fun j => MvPolynomial.eval u (g j).1\n   456\t\n   457\t/-- Quantum soundness obligation for the directly indexed low-degree game.\n   458\tThis is the repaired import form proposed in\n   459\t`docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility.tex`, needed by the Chapter 15\n   460\tcombining argument at paper\n   461\t`references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1267-1288`.\n   462\t\n   463\tThis is a formalization auxiliary assertion, not the source-labelled\n   464\t`lem:ld-soundness`.  Its proof must establish the game-correspondence and\n   465\tauxiliary-parameter bounds catalogued in the cited gap note; neither is hidden\n   466\tas a hypothesis here. -/\n   467\ttheorem exists_direct_ld_soundness :\n   468\t    ∃ a b : ℝ, 1 ≤ a ∧ 0 < b ∧ b ≤ 1 ∧\n   469\t      ∀ (D : DirectLdParams) (ε : ℝ), 0 < ε →\n   470\t        ∀ S : Strategy (directLdGame D), S.IsProjective → 1 - ε ≤ S.value →\n   471\t          ∃ GA : DirectPolyMeasTuple D S.ιA,\n   472\t            ∃ GB : DirectPolyMeasTuple D S.ιB,\n   473\t              consistencyDefect\n   474\t                  (uniformDistribution (Fin D.m → DirectScalarQ D))\n   475\t                  (fun u outcome =>\n   476\t                    heteroKron\n   477\t                      (((S.A (directLdPointQuestionOf D u)).postprocess\n   478\t                        (directLdPointValuesOrZero D)).effect outcome) 1)\n   479\t                  (fun u outcome =>\n   480\t                    heteroKron 1\n   481\t                      ((GB.postprocess (evalDirectPolyTupleAt u)).effect outcome))\n   482\t                  S.ψ ≤ deltaLd a b ε D.q D.m D.d D.k ∧\n   483\t              consistencyDefect\n   484\t                  (uniformDistribution (Fin D.m → DirectScalarQ D))\n   485\t                  (fun u outcome =>\n   486\t                    heteroKron\n   487\t                      ((GA.postprocess (evalDirectPolyTupleAt u)).effect outcome) 1)\n   488\t                  (fun u outcome =>\n   489\t                    heteroKron 1\n   490\t                      (((S.B (directLdPointQuestionOf D u)).postprocess\n   491\t                        (directLdPointValuesOrZero D)).effect outcome))\n   492\t                  S.ψ ≤ deltaLd a b ε D.q D.m D.d D.k ∧\n   493\t              consistencyDefect (uniformDistribution Unit)\n   494\t                  (fun _ g => heteroKron (GA.effect g) 1)\n   495\t                  (fun _ g => heteroKron 1 (GB.effect g))\n   496\t                  S.ψ ≤ deltaLd a b ε D.q D.m D.d D.k := by\n   497\t  sorry\n   498\t\n   499\tend\n   500\t\n   501\tend MIPStarRE.QPBT\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
