he question distribution named in the statement, with register placements indicated by subscripts; ``all symmetric equivalents'' refers to the register interchanges of Definition~\\ref{def:symmetric-equivalents}.\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex:276:We can now prove the soundness theorem for the Pauli basis test, stated as Theorem~\\ref{thm:pauli} in Chapter~\\ref{chap:qpbt-test}.\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex:292:\tThis invocation is where the analysis of the classical low individual degree test enters: Lemma~\\ref{lem:qld-unitary} rests on the polynomial-pair measurement of Lemma~\\ref{lem:qld-4-7}, whose proof instantiates the classical test in $2m+2$ variables and at present does so only when $2m+2$ divides $q$ --- a divisibility that fails for every admissible tuple with $m \\geq 2$. Three further steps of that same chain are likewise unproved. The classical soundness statement invoked there, Theorem~\\ref{lem:ld-soundness}, is imported from Theorem~4.7 of~\\cite{Ji2021Quantum} through an identification of the game $\\mathfrak{G}^{\\mathrm{ld}}_{(q,m,d,1)}$ with the two-prover tensor-code test for $\\code^{\\ot m}$, and neither that game correspondence nor the bound on the auxiliary parameter of Theorem~4.7 under which the stated error function $\\delta_{\\mathrm{ld}}$ is obtained has been established; both, with the divisibility obstruction, are documented in \\cite{gap:qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility}. Furthermore, the combined-lines consistency of Lemma~\\ref{lem:qld-4-13}, which Lemma~\\ref{lem:qld-4-7} consumes, is established here only with the error $m \\cdot \\poly(\\eps, md/q)$, the error form $\\poly(m^2 \\eps, md/q)$ carried in its statement remaining unproved (see \\cite{gap:qpbt_combined-lines-error-term}). The present proof is therefore complete only modulo these four obligations. Since the expanded state $\\ket{\\hat\\psi}$ of Definition~\\ref{def:expanded-state} is exactly $\\ket{\\psi}$ with the halves of $M$ pairs $\\ket{\\mathrm{EPR}_q}$ appended locally in registers $\\mathrm{A}'\\mathrm{A}''$ and $\\mathrm{B}'\\mathrm{B}''$, we have $\\phi_{\\mathrm{A}} \\ot \\phi_{\\mathrm{B}} \\ket{\\psi} = V_{\\mathrm{A}} \\ot V_{\\mathrm{B}} \\ket{\\hat\\psi}$. Lemma~\\ref{lem:qld-unitary} therefore yields a state $\\ket{\\mathrm{aux}}$ on registers $\\mathrm{A}\\mathrm{A}'\\mathrm{B}\\mathrm{B}'$ such that\ndocs/paper-gaps/qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility.tex:117:\\path{references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex},\ndocs/paper-gaps/qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility.tex:122:\\path{references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex},\ndocs/paper-gaps/qpbt_ld-sandwich-indexing.tex:52:\\path{blueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex}, lines~398--425, and explains\ndocs/paper-gaps/qpbt_symmetrization-attainment.tex:95:\\path{references/qpbt-paper/06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex}, lines~94--99,\ndocs/paper-gaps/qpbt_symmetrization-attainment.tex:98:\\path{blueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex}.}\ndocs/paper-gaps/qpbt_symmetrization-attainment.tex:158:\\footnote{\\path{references/qpbt-paper/10_oracularization.tex},\ndocs/paper-gaps/qpbt_symmetrization-attainment.tex:167:\\footnote{\\path{references/qpbt-paper/11_answer_reduction.tex},\ndocs/paper-gaps/qpbt_characteristic-two-pauli-scope.tex:77:\\path{blueprint/src/chapter/ch11_qpbt_algebra.tex}, lines~553--633 and\ndocs/paper-gaps/qpbt_characteristic-two-pauli-scope.tex:84:The separately named binary declarations are used by the later QPBT chapters.\ndocs/paper-gaps/qpbt_characteristic-two-pauli-scope.tex:94:the QPBT parameter regime.  The remaining work is to prove the general\ndocs/paper-gaps/qpbt_polynomial-error-square-root.tex:54:\\path{references/qpbt-paper/04_preliminaries.tex} and\ndocs/paper-gaps/qpbt_polynomial-error-square-root.tex:55:\\path{references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex}.  The\ndocs/paper-gaps/qpbt_polynomial-error-square-root.tex:74:\\doclink{MIPStarRE/QPBT/G