PStarRE.QPBT.SymmetricGame.toGame, MIPStarRE.QPBT.SymmetricStrategy, MIPStarRE.QPBT.SymmetricStrategy.toStrategy}\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:113:% Source statement (references/qpbt-paper/06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:94-99) kept in\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:117:\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.exists_symmetric_projective_strategy}\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:134:\tThe statement asserts more, namely a single symmetric projective strategy of value at least $1-\\eps$ itself. Passing from the family of strategies constructed above to one attaining the bound $1-\\eps$ is an attainment step which the argument does not supply: the supremum defining $\\operatorname{val}^*(\\mathfrak G)$ in Definition~\\ref{def:tensor-product-value} ranges over strategies of unbounded dimension and need not be attained. This step remains unproved; the obstruction, and the forms of the lemma that the argument does prove, are documented in \\cite{gap:qpbt_symmetrization-attainment}. See also Remark~\\ref{rem:symmetric-strat-limit}.\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:138:\tThe proof of Lemma~\\ref{lem:symmetric-strat} yields, for each $\\eps' > \\eps$, a symmetric projective strategy of value at least $1-\\eps'$. The conclusion as stated, at $\\eps' = \\eps$, does not follow from this: the dilated dimension $d$ may grow as $\\eps' \\downarrow \\eps$, and the supremum defining $\\operatorname{val}^*(\\mathfrak G)$ in Definition~\\ref{def:tensor-product-value} need not be attained by any strategy. The symmetrization construction itself is value-preserving, so the conclusion does hold whenever the hypothesis supplies an actual strategy of value at least $1-\\eps$ rather than only the value of the game; every use of the lemma in the source proceeds from such a strategy, or from a strict lower bound on the value, and therefore consumes only what the proof establishes. The gap and the available repairs are documented in \\cite{gap:qpbt_symmetrization-attainment}.\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:142:\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.IsCommutingOn, MIPStarRE.QPBT.Strategy.IsCommuting}\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:153:\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.Measurement.IsConsistentOn}\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:170:\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.IsConsistentStrategyOn, MIPStarRE.QPBT.SymmetricStrategy.IsConsistent}\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:179:\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.Strategy.IsPCC, MIPStarRE.QPBT.SymmetricStrategy.IsSPCC}\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:196:\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.consistencyDefect, MIPStarRE.QPBT.IsConsistentWithin}\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:212:% The source (references/qpbt-paper/06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:257-274) states this\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:229:\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.AreCloseStrategies}\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:246:\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.opFamilyDistSq_le_two_mul_consistencyDefect, MIPStarRE.QPBT.consistencyDefect_le_opFamilyDistSq_of_projective, MIPStarRE.QPBT.consistencyDefect_le_sqrt_of_projective_left}\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:261:\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.opFamilyDistSq_mul_left_le}\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:277:\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.opFamilyDistSq_mul_funIndexed_le}\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:288:\t% The source (references/qpbt-paper/06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:347-361) ends with\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:295:\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.opDistSq_sum_sub_mul_le_of_projective}\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:312:\t% (references/qpbt-paper/06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:364-380) elides this.\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:317:\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.opFamilyDistSq_le_of_le_of_le}\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:328:\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.consistencyDefect_trans_le}\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:342:\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.consistencyDefect_postprocess_le}\nblueprin