act head SHA is green and reviewed, then merge it.\\n     3\\t\\n     4\\tThe one script in the issue-lifecycle area that changes ``main``: the local\\n     5\\treplacement for GitHub's branch-protection rules, which upstream were server-side\\n     6\\tsettings no client could bypass.  A single-account repository has none — the owner can\\n     7\\talways press Merge — so the authority is this file.  It refuses by default, every\\n     8\\toverride is named, and ``gh_common.merge_pr`` merges through the REST ``sha`` guard,\\n     9\\twhich makes GitHub reject the call if the head moved meanwhile.\\n    10\\t\\n    11\\tEvery piece of evidence lives on GitHub, bound to the head SHA (issues-prs.md; the old\\n    12\\t``prs/`` registry is archived under ``results/telemetry/registry-archive/``):\\n    13\\t\\n    14\\t1. the PR is open, unmerged, not a draft;\\n    15\\t2. the primary worktree is clean and on the base, and the local branch tip is that\\n    16\\t   SHA — the merge must be of the bytes that were built here;\\n    17\\t3. the eight ``local-ci/<step>`` contexts (ci.sh:70) and ``local-ci/summary`` are\\n    18\\t   ``success`` on it.  A missing context blocks: GitHub's combined state reads\\n    19\\t   \\\"success\\\" for a commit carrying no statuses at all;\\n    20\\t4. a ``<!-- mipstarre-review pr=N head=SHA -->`` COMMENT review sits on that exact\\n    21\\t   commit id, its ``VERDICT:`` line is APPROVED (or COMMENTED with zero unchecked\\n    22\\t   findings), and ``local-review/summary`` is ``success`` (DESIGN.md:66-69) — one\\n    23\\t   account cannot self-APPROVE, so an adverse verdict travels in that status;\\n    24\\t5. no ``CHANGES_REQUESTED`` review sits on that SHA, from anyone;\\n    25\\t6. the fix loop is quiescent: no live autofix.sh lock.  The ``[codex-auto-fix]`` /\\n    26\\t   ``[codex-review-fix]`` commit count since the merge base is printed for the\\n    27\\t   record only — the iteration cap is autofix.sh's loop-termination bound and\\n    28\\t   carries no merge authority (issues-prs.md 3; EVOLUTION.md 2026-09-02);\\n    29\\t7. every issue this PR closes has no open sub-issue left.\\n    30\\t\\n    31\\t``--adjudicated`` waives gate 4's adverse verdict — nothing else — when an\\n    32\\t``ADJUDICATION`` comment names this exact head (review.md 12).  GitHub merges and\\n    33\\tcloses the linked issues itself, so no local bookkeeping can double-count.  The\\n    34\\tbest-effort tail then fast-forwards local ``main``, refreshes the\\n    35\\t``refs/remotes/origin/main`` alias the hooks and diff-based audits need in order not\\n    36\\tto self-disable (DESIGN.md:83-85), warms the cache and drops the branch.\\n    37\\t\\n    38\\tUsage: pr_merge.py N [--check-only | --dry-run] [--adjudicated] [--no-warm-cache]\\n    39\\t\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    40\\t\\n    41\\tfrom __future__ import annotations\\n    42\\t\\n    43\\timport argparse\\n    44\\timport os\\n    45\\timport re\\n    46\\timport subprocess\\n    47\\timport sys\\n    48\\tfrom pathlib import Path\\n    49\\t\\n    50\\tsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent))  # gh_common/wf_util sit here\\n    51\\timport gh_common  # noqa: E402\\n    52\\tfrom wf_util import (TITLE_LIMIT, LayerError, cache_root, default_repo_root,  # noqa: E402\\n    53\\t                     file_lock, lock_dir, sanitize, utcnow)\\n    54\\t\\n    55\\t#: ci.sh:70 ``STEP_NAMES`` verbatim, plus the roll-up ci.sh posts last.\\n    56\\tCI_STEPS = (\\\"build\\\", \\\"blueprint-render\\\", \\\"paper-gaps\\\", \\\"blueprint-sync\\\",\\n    57\\t            \\\"file-length\\\", \\\"proof-debt\\\", \\\"proof-evasion\\\", \\\"statement-origin\\\")\\n    58\\tCI_CONTEXTS = tuple(f\\\"local-ci/{step}\\\" for step in CI_STEPS) + (\\\"local-ci/summary\\\",)\\n    59\\tREVIEW_CONTEXT = \\\"local-review/summary\\\"\\n    60\\t\\n    61\\t#: Findings are task-list items; an unticked box is an open finding.  Kept compatible\\n    62\\t#: with review.sh's tally and autofix.sh's ledger read.\\n    63\\tUNCHECKED_FINDING_RE = re.compile(r\\\"^\\\\s*[-*]\\\\s*\\\\[ \\\\]\\\", re.MULTILINE)\\n    64\\tVERDICT_RE = re.compile(r\\\"^VERDICT:\\\\s*([A-Z_]+)\\\", re.MULTILINE)\\n    65\\t\\n    66\\t#: autofix.sh:62-63 ``PREFIX_AUTO``/``PREFIX_REVIEW`` — the ping-pong guard's subject\\n    67\\t#: prefixes; gate 6 reports how many such commits the PR carries.\\n    68\\tFIX_COMMIT_PREFIXES = (\\\"[codex-auto-fix]\\\", \\\"[codex-review-fix]\\\")\\n    69\\t\\n    70\\t#: GitHub's nine auto-closing keywords, exactly (close/closes/closed, fix/fixes/fixed,\\n    71\\t#: resolve/resolves/resolved) — the gate must see every issue GitHub will close on\\n    72\\t#: merge.  ``Addresses`` keeps an issue open and imposes no dependency\\n    73\\t#: (CONTRIBUTING.md:61-62).  Keep in sync with pr_open.py CLOSES_RE.\\n    74\\tCLOSES_RE = re.compile(r\\\"\\\\b(?:close[sd]?|fix(?:e[sd])?|resolve[sd]?):?\\\\s+#(\\\\d+)\\\", re.IGNORECASE)\\n    75\\t\\n    76\\t\\n    77\\tclass GateFailure(LayerError):\\n    78\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"A refusal to merge.  Distinct type so the caller can report it as such.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    79\\t\\n    80\\t\\n    81\\t# --------------------------------------------------------------- small helpers\\n    82\\t\\n    83\\tdef git(repo_root: Path, *args: str, check: bool = True) -> str:\\n    84\\t    result = subprocess.run([\\\"git\\\", *args], cwd=str(repo_root),\\n    85\\t                            capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\\n    86\\t    if check and result.returncode != 0:\\n    87\\t        raise LayerError(f\\\"git {' '.join(args)} failed ({result.returncode}): \\\"\\n    88\\t                         f\\\"{result.stderr.strip() or result.stdout.strip()}\\\")\\n    89\\t    return result.stdout.strip()\\n    90\\t\\n    91\\t\\n    92\\tdef git_ok(repo_root: Path, *args: str) -> bool:\\n    93\\t    return subprocess.run([\\\"git\\\", *args], cwd=str(repo_root), capture_output=True,\\n    94\\t                          text=True, check=False).returncode == 0\\n    95\\t\\n    96\\t\\n    97\\tdef _pid_alive(pid: int) -> bool:\\n    98\\t    try:\\n    99\\t        os.kill(pid, 0)\\n   100\\t    except ProcessLookupError:\\n   101\\t        return False\\n   102\\t    except PermissionError:\\n   103\\t        return True\\n   104\\t    return True\\n   105\\t\\n   106\\t\\n   107\\tdef passed(line: str) -> None:\\n   108\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"One line of the gate report, printed as the gate clears (--check-only reads).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   109\\t    sys.stdout.write(line + \\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n   110\\t\\n   111\\t\\n   112\\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------- gates\\n   113\\t\\n   114\\tdef ensure_mergeable_worktree(repo_root: Path, branch: str, base: str, head_sha: str) -> None:\\n   115\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Gate 2 — clean primary worktree on the base, local branch at the head.\\n   116\\t\\n   117\\t    GitHub performs the merge, so none of this is needed for the merge itself; all of it\\n   118\\t    is needed for the tail, which fast-forwards ``base`` in this very worktree and\\n   119\\t    deletes the branch.  Refusing here keeps the failure before the irreversible step.\\n   120\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   121\\t    dirty = git(repo_root, \\\"status\\\", \\\"--porcelain\\\")\\n   122\\t    if dirty:\\n   123\\t        raise GateFailure(\\\"gate 2 (worktree): the primary tree is not clean, required clean \\\"\\n   124\\t                          \\\"so the post-merge fast-forward cannot lose work:\\\\n\\\" + dirty)\\n   125\\t    current = git(repo_root, \\\"rev-parse\\\", \\\"--abbrev-ref\\\", \\\"HEAD\\\")\\n   126\\t    if current != base:\\n   127\\t        raise GateFailure(f\\\"gate 2 (worktree): HEAD is on {current!r}, required {base!r} \\\"\\n   128\\t                          f\\\"(the PR base). Run: git switch {base}\\\")\\n   129\\t    tip = git(repo_root, \\\"rev-parse\\\", \\\"--verify\\\", f\\\"{branch}